# Commit discipline

Every discrete implementation or fix in Entropy gets its **own git commit**, even when small.

## Rules

- Do **not** batch unrelated features into one commit.
- Prefer a short series of focused commits over one large commit.
- Commit message style: `feat:` / `fix:` / `docs:` / `refactor:` — explain **why**, match existing repo tone.
- Never add `Co-authored-by` trailers unless the user asks.
- When the user asks for multiple features or a roadmap slice, implement **one by one**: finish, commit, then start the next.
- After each implementation the user requested under this workflow, **commit before starting the next feature** (do not wait for a separate “please commit” if they already asked for commit-per-feature).
- Only skip committing when the user explicitly says not to commit yet.

## Examples of separate commits

- Treemap hover intel
- Titlebar path navigation
- Folder card size display
- Content-hash duplicates
- Duplicate scope chooser
- Safe delete preview

Do not combine those into a single commit.
